@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Export sessions as Agent Session Record
+
+Export one saved session to standard output:
+
+```sh
+qwen sessions export --format agent-session --session SESSION_ID
+```
+
+Use `--output DIRECTORY` for separate private JSONL files. Files are named with
+SHA-256 hashes of session IDs. Existing files are refused. Each file retains the
+native identity in its header. `--session` can repeat with directory output.
+Without `--session`, directory output selects all sessions in the current
+project. `--since` accepts an RFC 3339 timestamp and selects by source file
+modification time.
+
+Use `--input FILE` to read a specific native transcript. This option can repeat.
+It bypasses project discovery and does not read global configuration. A missing
+source, duplicate session identity or ambiguous standard output is an error.
+
+The exporter writes ASR 0.1 with `producer.method: native`. It preserves recorded
+text, tool arguments, model-facing results and source order. It folds result
+updates at their final observation. A rewind does not erase retained work.
+Malformed lines and incomplete tails produce gaps. Missing times and outcomes
+stay unknown. Native integers outside the safe JavaScript range become strings.
+
+Approvals, complete settings, model-call accounting, offered tools, file-change
+normalization, commits, instruction context and copy detection are declared
+missing. No inference is invented from a message boundary. No approval is
+inferred from a tool outcome. Qwen preserves recorded approval policy updates, prompt-time approval mode, custom titles and explicit parent-session links. Managed transaction journals are refused. Legacy chat recordings are supported.
+
+Known credential fields, credential patterns, secret values present in the
+exporter's environment and opaque provider signatures are excluded. Exclusion
+marks shortened records and declares losses. Review exports before sharing.
+This filter cannot recognize every secret in arbitrary prose.
+
+This change provides an offline export command. It does not write live ASR,
+install a discovery file or change native recording. A discovery file can use
+`["qwen", "sessions", "export", "--format", "agent-session"]` as its
+`exportCommand`, with `formatVersions: ["0.1"]` and
+`supportsDeletionHook: false`. Consumers still supply a selector or output path.
