+# Native Agent Session Record export
+
+[English](agent-session-export.md) | [简体中文](agent-session-export.zh-CN.md)
+
+## Problem and current state
+
+Saved legacy transcripts expose messages and tool results through native
+`ChatRecord` values. There is no ASR export subcommand. Collectors need a stable
+session identity and an ordered stream without starting a model session.
+
+## Proposed changes
+
+Add `sessions export --format agent-session`. A CLI-local projection reads
+complete JSONL lines and uses the native record types. It preserves retained
+branches, folds duplicate tool results at completion and records source policy
+updates. A small helper handles content parts, IDs, secret exclusion and output.
+No core runtime code changes.
+
+## Decisions and scope
+
+Explicit `--input` files bypass configuration. Default discovery uses the
+existing project session service and includes archived transcripts. One selector
+writes to standard output. Directory exports use hashed filenames and exclusive
+private writes. File modification times implement `--since`.
+
+Only recorded human provenance establishes human authorship. Missing model-call
+boundaries, approvals, full settings, instructions, usage, file changes, commits
+and copy detection remain declared losses. No current Git state, account identity
+or configuration is borrowed as historical evidence. Managed journals are
+rejected because their transaction protocol needs a separate mapping.
+
+## Risks and validation
+
+Arbitrary prose can contain secrets that a filter cannot recognize. Exports
+must be reviewed before sharing. Source data is untrusted and never executed.
+Malformed lines and incomplete tails produce gaps. Native large integers remain
+exact strings. Tests cover mapping, order, corruption, secret exclusion, output
+selection and private files. Synthetic scratch sessions exercise the local
+model endpoint. The ASR validator checks each final sample with zero errors.
+
+## Acceptance and open questions
+
+The command emits deterministic ASR 0.1 with native producer identity. Focused
+tests and validation pass. Existing sessions commands retain their behavior.
+Live ASR, managed journals and automatic discovery registration are out of scope.
+There are no open implementation questions.
